## Delivered boundary

Bounded nonphysical presence, authorized spatial/semantic queries and captured multi-selection with per-source grants.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Shared subscription/query transport, view/presence codecs and permission projection.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 03.T05

- [ ] **03.T05.** Carry canonical/local-frame identity through the participant view/presence envelope. Implement optional bounded cursor/selection and lightweight-avatar presentation state using I2/I5/I6, with session sequence/expiry and visible opt-out/follow behavior. Reuse view-local origins and keep shared camera bindings explicit; B36 first proves independent views, correct pose/selection mapping, release and no accepted geometry/physical-body mutation.

### Task 04.T05

- [ ] **04.T05.** Extend existing policy and E4 queries to the model/occurrence/property scopes needed here and authorized spatial/semantic interests. Prove B34/B36 server-side denial for metadata, selection, bounds and partial asset/source references before delivery, including a public guest and a narrower identified viewer. Reuse the same query/anchor path for hosted mounted Sands and Areas; shared visibility never lends operational/host authority. Prepare B40's captured multi-selection/scope and authorized matching-copy queries without a full-world scan. Preserve per-occurrence state and distinguish a selected-set edit from a deliberate shared-definition update.

